      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "**The latest major release from xAI is Grok 4.6**, which launched on August 12, 2026.[[1]](https://r.jina.ai/https:/x.ai/blog)\n\n### Key Details on Grok 4.6\n- It focuses on improvements for long-running agents, coding, knowledge work, interactive and visual tasks, with a 500,000-token context window.[[2]](https://letsdatascience.com/news/topic/grok)\n- Benchmarks: It scores approximately 60.92–61 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index, nearly tying OpenAI’s GPT-5.6 Sol Max (one of the top frontier models at the time).[[3]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n- Pricing (API): Around $2 per million input tokens and $6 per million output tokens.[[3]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n- It has been rolled out to various platforms, including GitHub Copilot (August 14), Amazon Bedrock, Microsoft Foundry, Google Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform, and others in the weeks following release.[[4]](https://updatealert.io/updates/x-ai)\n\n### Upcoming: Grok 4.7\nElon Musk announced on September 2, 2026, that **Grok 4.7 is expected in about 10 days** (around September 12, 2026).[[5]](https://cryptorank.io/news/feed/db1bc-grok-4-7-release-spacex-data)\n- It will scale up to 2.1 trillion parameters (from 1.5T in 4.6).\n- Training incorporates unique SpaceX data, with claims it will surpass all current models, especially in real-world engineering.\n- It is described as slightly slower but more token-efficient than 4.6.[[6]](https://m.economictimes.com/tech/artificial-intelligence/elon-musk-teases-grok-4-6-and-4-7-doubling-down-on-xais-rapid-fire-releases/articleshow/132693365.cms)\n\nOther recent updates include Grok Voice 2.0 (August 5), Grok Bot (agent features), image/video generation improvements, and various platform integrations, but the flagship model remains Grok 4.6 until 4.7 arrives.[[3]](https://tesorb.com/command/xai/)\n\nFor the most up-to-date information, check x.ai/blog or Elon Musk’s/X account, as xAI moves quickly.",
